    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "When the critical power source that failed the community—Kepco SPC Power's Unit 2—went offline, a massive power shortage affecting countless homes followed. The cascading failure began with this equipment failure, leaving the region's energy deficit at over 950 megawatts. Protecting the vulnerable system required urgent action: emergency measures to prevent a wider blackout were implemented through load shedding.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Caregiver",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-2",
          "result-0"
        ],
        "center": "result-0",
        "channel": "toned",
        "channel_role": "toned",
        "composition_mode": "ADR-0008",
        "salience_rank": 0
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.85
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The vulnerable energy suppliers left exposed—eleven generators—saw their capacity diminished by prolonged neglect of critical infrastructure. Dangerous heatwave stressing the vulnerable system drove demand pressure, exposing the grid's fragility. Officials, as protective authorities managing the crisis, worked to stabilize the power grid amidst this threat.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Caregiver",
        "fragments": [
          "why-1",
          "why-2",
          "how-1"
        ],
        "center": "who-3",
        "channel": "toned",
        "channel_role": "toned",
        "composition_mode": "ADR-0008",
        "salience_rank": 2
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.78
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "From the perspective of the Philippines grid operator, the duty to protect the grid's stability was paramount. After the unit's unexpected shutdown triggered a grid incident, the power system overseer declared a red alert for the Visayas region. This emergency response aimed to manage the thin operating margin caused by high demand, implementing grid stabilization measures to prevent a broader collapse.",
      "source": {
